      "answer": "$x=-0.618$ (3 d.p.).",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "State that $1+e^{-3x}=e^2$ — B1, with no errors seen to that point.\n\nUse a correct method to solve an equation of the form $e^{-3x}=a$, where $a>0$, for $x$, or equivalent — M1. Here $e^{-3x}=e^2-1=6.389\\ldots$; evidence of method must be seen.\n\nObtain $x=-0.618$ only — A1. Must be 3 decimal places.\n\nAlternative method: state that $1+e^{-3x}=e^2$ — B1; rearrange to obtain an expression for $e^x$ and solve an equation of the form $e^x=a$, where $a>0$, or equivalent — M1, e.g. $e^x=\\sqrt[3]{1/(e^2-1)}$; obtain $x=-0.618$ only — A1, must be 3 decimal places.\n\nTotal [3].",
